# Confirm the complete list of software authors before publication.
# The listed author is provisionally identified from the repository owner's public profile.
# After Zenodo archives v1.0.0, add its version-specific DOI with the `doi` key.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Grid Reprojector in research, please cite the archived software release."
title: "Grid Reprojector"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - given-names: "Lorenzo"
    family-names: "Gianquintieri"
    affiliation: "Politecnico di Milano"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9658-5749"
abstract: >-
  Grid Reprojector is a standalone PyQGIS application for transferring
  numerical data between polygon grids. It supports single-file, batch,
  and time-series workflows, intensive and extensive variables,
  area-based areal interpolation, and alternative weighting in
  single-file and batch modes.
repository-code: "https://github.com/LGpolimi/pyqgis_gridreprojector"
url: "https://github.com/LGpolimi/pyqgis_gridreprojector"
# Non-standard license: use license-url, not an invented SPDX license identifier.
license-url: "https://github.com/LGpolimi/pyqgis_gridreprojector/blob/main/LICENSE.txt"
keywords:
  - PyQGIS
  - GIS
  - areal interpolation
  - spatial harmonization
  - polygon grids
  - area weighting
  - geospatial analysis
